# Intervals
An **interval** is the distance between two notes, counted by letters with both ends included: C to D is a **2nd**, C to E a **3rd**, C to F a **4th**, C to G a **5th**. On the staff you can see it without naming every note:

- a **2nd** goes from a line to the space next to it, or a space to the line next to it (a step);
- a **3rd** from a line to the next line, or a space to the next space (a skip);
- a **4th** from a line to a space, or a space to a line, further apart;
- a **5th** from a line to the line two up, or a space to the space two up.

Reading the distance instead of naming every note is how players read fast. Each card is two notes, going up or down; when it's done, its name. **Look it up** (📖) has them all drawn.
